{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "t001",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# 05 · TESTING LAB — evidence room",
      "x": -1200,
      "y": -1550,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#0f766e"
    },
    {
      "id": "t002",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## **27 firmware environments build. 0 physical results are recorded. 10 backend tests pass.**\nThose two sentences are the whole point of this room.\n[[05 - Testing Lab/Testing Lab.md]]",
      "x": -1200,
      "y": -1380,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 150,
      "color": "#0f766e"
    },
    {
      "id": "g003",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "THE FIVE KINDS OF “IT WORKS”  —  never blur these",
      "x": -1200,
      "y": -1150,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 460,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t004",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**BUILD PASS** — the image compiles and links  ·  NOT that any part exists",
      "x": -1170,
      "y": -1070,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 84,
      "color": "#15803d"
    },
    {
      "id": "t005",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**SOFTWARE PASS** — a function returns the expected result on synthetic input  ·  NOT that the hardware path is sound",
      "x": -1170,
      "y": -978,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 84,
      "color": "#6d28d9"
    },
    {
      "id": "t006",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**UNVERIFIED** — the firmware issued the command; nobody saw the effect  ·  NOT that the LED lit",
      "x": -1170,
      "y": -886,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 84,
      "color": "#92400e"
    },
    {
      "id": "t007",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**PASS** — a person ran it AND saw the expected physical result  ·  —",
      "x": -1170,
      "y": -794,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 84,
      "color": "#15803d"
    },
    {
      "id": "t008",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**BLOCKED** — a prerequisite prevents the test  ·  nothing at all",
      "x": -1170,
      "y": -702,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 84,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "g009",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "ENFORCED IN CODE",
      "x": -1200,
      "y": -660,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#15803d"
    },
    {
      "id": "f010",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "firmware/include/test_result.h",
      "x": -1170,
      "y": -600,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 100,
      "color": "#15803d"
    },
    {
      "id": "t011",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "`TestResult::finish()` cannot return **PASS** when checks were skipped or a test called `unverified()`. Buzzer tests *must* land in UNVERIFIED — GPIO code cannot sense its own effect. (OLED/LEDs removed from this project.)",
      "x": -1170,
      "y": -480,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 100,
      "color": "#92400e"
    },
    {
      "id": "g012",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "COMPONENT ENVIRONMENTS  —  15 build, 0 executed",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -1550,
      "width": 2300,
      "height": 700,
      "color": "#0f766e"
    },
    {
      "id": "t013",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`esp32_core`**\nchip · CPU · heap · flash · reset",
      "x": 30,
      "y": -1470,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t014",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`uart1_loopback`**\nGPIO25 TX → GPIO26 RX jumper",
      "x": 595,
      "y": -1470,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t015",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`uart2_loopback`**\nsame on UART2",
      "x": 1160,
      "y": -1470,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t016",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`r307s`**\nread-only VerifyPassword/ReadSysPara/TemplateCount",
      "x": 1725,
      "y": -1470,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t017",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`i2c_scan`**\nsweeps addresses 1–126 on 21/22",
      "x": 30,
      "y": -1340,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t018",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`oled`**\ntext · pixel · line · clear · refresh",
      "x": 595,
      "y": -1340,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t019",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`rtc`**\nACK · advancing time · lostPower. **never writes the clock**",
      "x": 1160,
      "y": -1340,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t020",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`green_led`**\nGPIO18 off/on/blink",
      "x": 1725,
      "y": -1340,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t021",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`red_led`**\nGPIO19 off/on/blink",
      "x": 30,
      "y": -1210,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t022",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`buzzer`**\nGPIO23 two 80 ms beeps",
      "x": 595,
      "y": -1210,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t023",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`gpio_sanity`**\ninputs only · drives nothing · shorts nothing",
      "x": 1160,
      "y": -1210,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t024",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`wifi_diag`**\nscan without logging SSIDs",
      "x": 1725,
      "y": -1210,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t025",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`backend_http`**\nGET /health · **sends no attendance record**",
      "x": 30,
      "y": -1080,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t026",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`json`**\nsynthetic payload round-trip",
      "x": 595,
      "y": -1080,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t027",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`storage`**\nmount without formatting · CRC · cleanup",
      "x": 1160,
      "y": -1080,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t028",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`power_reset`**\nreset reason · boot time · **measures no voltage**",
      "x": 1725,
      "y": -1080,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t029",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Each environment is `build_src_filter = -<*> +<one file>`, so exactly one `setup()/loop()` compiles.",
      "x": 30,
      "y": -960,
      "width": 2260,
      "height": 90,
      "color": "#0f766e"
    },
    {
      "id": "g030",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "INTEGRATION ENVIRONMENTS  —  9 build, 0 executed · one file, `-D INTEGRATION_CASE=1..9`",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -820,
      "width": 2300,
      "height": 620,
      "color": "#0f766e"
    },
    {
      "id": "t031",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**INT-01 — RTC** · `int_rtc`\nESP32 + RTC",
      "x": 30,
      "y": -740,
      "width": 710,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t032",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**INT-02** · `int_rtc`\nESP32 + RTC",
      "x": 780,
      "y": -740,
      "width": 710,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t033",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**INT-03** · `int_outputs`\nESP32 + LEDs + buzzer",
      "x": 1530,
      "y": -740,
      "width": 710,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t034",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**INT-04** · `int_r307s`\nESP32 + R307S read-only",
      "x": 30,
      "y": -610,
      "width": 710,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t035",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**INT-03 — RTC+R307S** · `int_r307s_rtc`\nR307S + RTC",
      "x": 780,
      "y": -610,
      "width": 710,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t036",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**INT-06** · `int_r307s_rtc`\nR307S + RTC",
      "x": 1530,
      "y": -610,
      "width": 710,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t037",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**INT-07** · `int_wifi`\nESP32 + Wi-Fi",
      "x": 30,
      "y": -480,
      "width": 710,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t038",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**INT-08** · `int_backend`\nESP32 + backend /health",
      "x": 780,
      "y": -480,
      "width": 710,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t039",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**INT-09** · `int_full`\neverything except the attendance workflow",
      "x": 1530,
      "y": -480,
      "width": 710,
      "height": 118,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t040",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### INT-10 · `production` — the only test that would prove the product\nenrollment → live POST → outage → reboot → replay. **Never run.** The queue's crash/replay claims stay unverified until it is.",
      "x": 30,
      "y": -330,
      "width": 2190,
      "height": 130,
      "color": "#0891b2"
    },
    {
      "id": "g041",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "BACKEND  —  10 tests, PASSING",
      "x": -1200,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 380,
      "color": "#6d28d9"
    },
    {
      "id": "f042",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "backend/tests/test_api.py",
      "x": -1170,
      "y": 260,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 100,
      "color": "#6d28d9"
    },
    {
      "id": "f043",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "backend/tests/test_database.py",
      "x": -1170,
      "y": 380,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 100,
      "color": "#6d28d9"
    },
    {
      "id": "t044",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "`cd backend && .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest tests -q`  →  **10 passed** in 0.79 s",
      "x": -1170,
      "y": 500,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "#15803d"
    },
    {
      "id": "t045",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Synthetic fixtures in temporary SQLite databases. Covers the contract, the migration path, constraints, idempotency and the 60-second boundary.\n**A green backend suite says nothing about the wire between the ESP32 and the laptop.**",
      "x": -1170,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#92400e"
    },
    {
      "id": "g046",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "SENSOR EVIDENCE  —  the only physical results that exist anywhere in this project",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -80,
      "width": 2300,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t047",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-02 → HW-03 → HW-11 → HW-13**\n0 bytes @ 57600 · 0 bytes at all 12 documented bauds · 0 bytes with software-swapped routing · GPIO32 line reads **driven high**\n→ baud EXCLUDED · crossed wires EXCLUDED · the wire is not floating",
      "x": 30,
      "y": -10,
      "width": 1090,
      "height": 190,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t048",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**NOT EXECUTED**\nHW-05 ReadSysPara · HW-06 TemplateCount — both gated on receiving any valid ACK\nHW-10 USB pad path — pads unverified, no equipment\n→ **capacity is therefore still unknown. Do not provision from 1000 or 300.**",
      "x": 1170,
      "y": -10,
      "width": 1090,
      "height": 190,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "g049",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "R307S EVIDENCE CHAIN  —  detail lives in the Research Archive",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 640,
      "width": 2300,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t050",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-01**\nwiring topology\n[WIRED, voltage unmeasured]",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 235,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#92400e"
    },
    {
      "id": "t051",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-02**\n@ 57600\n[TX 16 B → RX 0 B]",
      "x": 285,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 235,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t052",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-03**\n12-baud ladder\n[0 bytes at every rate]",
      "x": 540,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 235,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t053",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-04**\nVerifyPassword\n[0 bytes]",
      "x": 795,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 235,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t054",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-05/06**\nReadSysPara / count\n[NOT EXECUTED — gated on an ACK]",
      "x": 1050,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 235,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t055",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-08**\nunsolicited data\n[0 transitions in 1.5 s]",
      "x": 1305,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 235,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t056",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-10**\nUSB pads\n[NOT EXECUTED — unverified order]",
      "x": 1560,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 235,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t057",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-11**\nswapped routing\n[0 bytes @ 57600 and 9600]",
      "x": 1815,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 235,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t058",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-13**\nRX line-state\n[driven high, ~2822 mV estimate]",
      "x": 2070,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 235,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#92400e"
    },
    {
      "id": "t059",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**The 3.3 V solder jumper is the leading unmeasured suspect.** 5 V into a shorted jumper kills the module silently, and no software test can see it. `HW-00` (measure) is BLOCKED on the absence of a multimeter.",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 830,
      "width": 2190,
      "height": 100,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
